{
  "id": "plr_menu",
  "kind": "object",
  "type": "player",
  "name": "Menu monster",
  "notes": "The monster that walks the menu map: the current pick ('chosen', Furrbit the Normal type on a fresh save), in its own look (a shiny one shimmers). The D-pad walks it in 8 directions over the 7 x 7 screens of the map (the camera shows one whole screen and jumps to the next when its middle crosses an edge). It is a level-7 monster with all 3 moves: outside the Green Meadow A, B and R fire them (map_moves), with HP like a level-7 monster in a run (108, Furrbit 120, shiny 132 / 149, +5 per garden HP UP: map_hp_max) and the garden's POWER UPs (map_power), +20% power when shiny; floor items, won items and waves cards belong to the runs. The fights follow the run rules (type chart, MISS, statuses, the walking dodge, each species' traits, the low-HP beep). At 0 HP it faints: it blinks out, the screen fades and it wakes up in the Meadow with full HP (the menu scene loads again; nothing opened is lost). In the Meadow A or B by a sign picks it (CLASSIC starts the classic run, WAVES the waves run once all 9 monsters are freed, CLEAR SAVE asks), the sign's name shows over its head, R does nothing, and walking back into the Meadow refills its HP. It walks out of the cave on its own (enter_ticks) after the picker.",
